      "id": 50918,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-01-02T18:27:33.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Aww, when you said \"English\", I thought you meant…well, you know, English ;).Can all of you guys move over to somewhere in the southeast of England so I can actually play Sentinels with more than one person at a time? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Do you have a local game store? Maybe you could find some other players by working with the staff to organize a game day. If you get the staff interested in the game, they are reasonably likely to suggest it to customers.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
